<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to May 10.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to May 10.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to May 10 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week May 4-May 10</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,592,299 tns	172,259 tns    10.82 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,582,125 tns	178,418 tns    11.28 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,583,554 tns	172,272 tns    10.88 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to May 10</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    37,009.085 tns    4,006,110 tns    10.82 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    37,130,527 tns    4,040,856 tns    10.88 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    35,204,824 tns    3,762,658 tns    10.69 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 57 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 57 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 57 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
</text>
